; Example usage of the `head-counts` plugin — the documents that satisfy
; every bound. The three that *break* one are siblings, so this file stays
; a valid document (the schema-export round-trip feeds it to ajv):
;
;   example-too-many.sjon   over a `:max`
;   example-missing.sjon    under a `:min`
;   example-open.sjon       both, on an `:open true` form
;
; One vertex (`:min 1 :max 1`), one fragment (`:max 1`), and two constants
; (unbounded).

(render-pipeline :name main
  (vertex   :entry vs_main)
  (fragment :entry fs_main)
  (constant :name gamma    :value 2.2)
  (constant :name exposure :value 1.0))

; The `:max 1` heads are ceilings, not requirements. A depth-only pass has
; no fragment stage and no constants — also clean, because `vertex` is the
; only head carrying a floor.

(render-pipeline :name depth-only
  (vertex :entry vs_depth))

; The same `pipeline-section` kind on a KEYED slot. `:max 1` is trivially
; satisfied there (a keyed slot holds one value) and `:min 1` has no set to
; be missing from, so neither count fires — this is the scope rule, and it
; is why a bounded kind stays shareable. The head-set's *narrowing* still
; applies: `(section-holder :section (nope))` would be `not_head_member`.
; It is only the counts that go quiet.

(section-holder :section (fragment :entry fs_main))
